From 8307999cc0376a1ce6dfe70ad6da738cdad82044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raiju contributors <raiju@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:30:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: TLS ALPN for client sockets: tls.alpn offers protocols,
 socket.alpnProtocol reads the one picked

A TLS client could not offer application protocols, so a client that needs one (gRPC
needs h2 in ALPN) could only reach a plaintext server. Bun.connect's tls option takes
alpn, the list of protocols offered, and the socket's alpnProtocol is the one the server
picked, or "" when it picked none (and for plaintext sockets). Without alpn the TLS
context keeps its default protocols, as before.

The offer is set on the SSL object before the handshake. Resumed sessions are keyed by the
offer too, so a session from one offer is not used for another.

Tests: tests/run/native_alpn.tov offers h2 and http/1.1, and offers nothing, to a TLS
listener and checks that the handshake succeeds and alpnProtocol reads "".
